---
title: 🥒 Tzatziki
servings: 6
source: https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2015/aug/06/how-to-make-perfect-tzatziki-felicity-cloake
tags:
  - greek
  - dip
  - yoghurt
  - sauce
---

-- ============================================================
-- PREP
-- ============================================================

If time allows, put the @whole-milk Greek yoghurt{500%g} (preferably ewe's milk) in a #sieve{} suspended above a #bowl{} and leave to drain for ~draining{2%hours}.

Meanwhile, crush the @garlic{4%cloves} (more or less to taste) into the @extra-virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} with a pinch of @salt{} and leave to infuse.

Coarsely grate the @cucumber{1/2} (half a large one) with a #grater{} and put it in a #colander{} in the sink. Salt lightly, toss and leave to drain for ~salting{30%minutes}.

-- ============================================================
-- COMBINE
-- ============================================================

Stir the garlicky oil and @white wine vinegar{1%tbsp} (or lemon juice) into the yoghurt. Squeeze out the cucumber very well, then stir this in too.

Allow to sit for ~resting{2%hours}, but preferably overnight.

Just before serving, season to taste, adding more oil or vinegar if necessary. Finely chop the @dill{1%small bunch} (or mint), discarding the tough stems, and stir into the tzatziki.
